# Shell / sandbox

When running any of these, always use Shell with `required_permissions: ["all"]`
(do not rely on the default sandbox):

- `./scripts/test.sh`
- `./scripts/dev-start.sh`
- `./scripts/dev-stop.sh`

Reason: they need process signals (kill) and/or writes under `/Volumes`.
`format.sh`, `build.sh`, and `install-dependency.sh` may stay sandboxed.
